  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of young boys in red soccer uniforms playing soccer on a grassy field. The text overlay reads \"he won because he is a boy\" at the top and \"competing in a female sport\" at the bottom. The overall intent of this meme is to promote a misogynistic and sexist message by implying that male athletes inherently dominate or succeed in sports that are traditionally associated with women, suggesting that their victory is due to their gender rather than skill or merit. This is a harmful and toxic message that reinforces gender stereotypes and diminishes the achievements of female athletes by implying that men are superior in sports by virtue of their gender. The meme uses the juxtaposition of the image of boys playing soccer with the text to create a false equivalence and to demean the legitimacy of women's sports, thereby contributing to a misogynistic worldview that devalues women's athletic abilities and achievements.",
